    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which requirements methodology — the fork this detection now carries",
      "prov:value": "**Detecting a feature request no longer selects CRDM by itself.** Since\n2026-09-21 (issue #730, the owner's option A) there are **two** parallel\nrequirements methodologies, and `methodology-adoption` forbids blending them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#730",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which requirements methodology — the fork this detection now carries",
      "prov:value": "The owner's words, 2026-09-21: *\"CRDM stays for stkaeholder facing WHO/IG\nwork…..spec-kit is specific to folio assistant feature development requests by\ntool developers not content developers (content agnostic, more scrum methodology\nprocess) for best practives of software development\"*.\n\n**Most of the signals listed below are now spec-kit's**, not CRDM's — the\n\"Platform-level change requests\" and \"Direct capability requests\" categories\nespecially, since both describe somebody building the tooling.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which requirements methodology — the fork this detection now carries",
      "prov:value": "**Most of the signals listed below are now spec-kit's**, not CRDM's — the\n\"Platform-level change requests\" and \"Direct capability requests\" categories\nespecially, since both describe somebody building the tooling."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A request for a plan",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-07 (issue #2405): *\"if we make a request for a plan you should\nALWAYS have created a requirements document and work plan for us to review\nbefore implementation.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2405",
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A request for a plan",
      "prov:value": "requests are not exempt** (decision 2 of 2026-10-07): \"plan the edits to\nchapter 3\" triggers it as surely as \"plan the new validator\". The fork above\nstill decides WHOSE requirements — this signal never selects a methodology\nand never blends them. What happens on a plan request is the same operation\nfor both, and it lives in the content layer above this one, which is why it is\nnamed here rather than linked —\nthe `plan-request-gate` skill (`skill_fetch plan-request-gate`)\n— produce a requirements document",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Self-declared genre",
      "prov:value": "Anchored to the opening line, and the reason has CHANGED. The anchor was\nchosen because an unanchored `proposal` also caught #187, a request to write\nup a merged proposal's changes, which was labelled *not* a feature request. On\n2026-09-24 the owner relabelled #187 a feature request, after a blind second\nannotation (bean `vjbl`): it is the change register for pipeline changes not\nyet built. Measured on the adjudicated corpus, the unanchored pattern now adds\nno false alarm and catches #187, which the anchor misses (recall 95.5% →\n100%). The anchor is kept until the owner decides, because changing a detector\nto fit its own 27-item eval set is tuning to the test.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vjbl",
        "#187",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A feature is a COLLABORATION you are joining, not a fix you are making",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-21, and this is the framing the rest of this file sits inside:\n\n> when agent in discussion with human and a feature comes up, it starts or\n> engages w/ existing collaborative design requiremnts between this user,\n> other users/authors/etc. other agents. treat the design/feature process as\n> such. it's not a one off fix... put it into epcis/stories.etc.\n> update/create needed artefacts and link to them under the appropriate\n> harnesse's docs/ page.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What to do instead",
      "prov:value": "**4. Write the artefacts, and LINK them from `docs/`.** The owner's\ninstruction is specific and it is the part most often skipped: *\"update/create\nneeded artefacts and link to them under the appropriate harnesse's docs/\npage.\"*\n\nAn artefact nobody can navigate to is an artefact nobody will read. The\nharness that owns the capability owns the link"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Related work first",
      "prov:value": "The procedure is [`related-work-coordination`](../sdlc-core/related-work-coordination.md), and `crdm-issue-linking.bpmn` calls it as `Process_RelatedWork` (issue #1023).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1023"
      ]
    }
